          53 text CAPABILITIES
          54 heading What Your Chama Can Do
          56 paragraph
            57 text Modern financial management designed for Kenyan table-banking and savings groups.
        58 article
          59 heading Clear contribution records
          61 paragraph
            62 text Record contributions and keep each member’s balance visible alongside the group’s shared records.
        63 article
          64 heading Savings and loan records
          66 paragraph
            67 text Keep contribution schedules, loan requests, repayments, and outstanding balances organized together.
        68 article
          69 heading Digital Governance
          71 paragraph
            72 text Support group decisions with meeting attendance, officer roles, loan approvals, and recorded rules.
        73 article
          74 heading Security & Transparency
          76 paragraph
            77 text PIN-protected, role-scoped access and an application audit log support review. The log is not tamper-evident, so keep source receipts and backups.
        78 article
          79 heading A clearer month-end close
          81 paragraph
            82 text Bring recorded cash contributions, repayments, open loan balances, and items needing attention into one read-only monthly view. Compare it with receipts and statements yourself; the app does not verify settlement or move funds.
        83 article
          84 heading Group chat, in context
          86 paragraph
            87 text Active chama members can discuss within their group. Messages refresh through live updates with polling recovery when the connection drops; this is not a WhatsApp or SMS broadcast.
